From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:29:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Android build: Kotlin/Gradle compile errors

- app/build.gradle: enable buildFeatures.buildConfig so BuildConfig is
  generated (NetworkModule.kt references BuildConfig.DEBUG).
- NativeActivity.kt: installSplashScreen() is a Kotlin top-level
  extension function, not a static method on SplashScreen -
  SplashScreen.installSplashScreen(this) is Java-interop syntax and
  doesn't resolve from Kotlin. Import the function directly and call
  it bare.
- BottomNavBar.kt: add the missing androidx.compose.runtime.getValue
  import needed for the `by navController.currentBackStackEntryAsState()`
  delegate.
- CertificateScreen.kt: rememberGraphicsLayer lives in
  androidx.compose.ui.graphics, not androidx.compose.ui.graphics.layer -
  fix the import path.
- CheckoutScreen.kt: drop the stray
  `import androidx.compose.foundation.layout.weight` - weight() is a
  RowScope/ColumnScope member, not a top-level import. Under the K2
  compiler that import resolves to an internal property instead of
  being silently ignored, which broke Modifier.weight(1f) usage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
